Changing the type of monster after it has been generated does not
change its inventory.  For example, wolves don't start with elven
boots, changing a wolf into an foo-elf does not mean the dead wolf-
turned-elf is going to drop elven boots just because elves often start
with them.  Death drops, however, are a different matter.  To increase
your likelihood of something useful from a death drop then you need a
(preferably not tiny) monster that leaves a corpse.   And IIRC death
drops call for a random object so go somewhere in the dungeon that has
a higher percentage chance of the random object being what you want.

